  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale:\nThe core idea is to use a multi-resolution optimization strategy combined with simulated annealing to globally explore the search space. This method balances between sparse and dense representations of the function. Unlike local optimization methods that often get stuck in poor local minima, this approach uses coarse grids for global exploration and fine grids for local refinement. The rationale is that the optimal function likely has a piecewise constant structure with few active intervals, so coarse grids can efficiently capture the global shape while fine grids provide high-fidelity adjustments.\n\nThe representation is piecewise constant on grid points, and the optimization shifts between different grid resolutions to find an effective transition point between 0 and 1. This method automatically handles the constraint enforcement through projection functions and explicitly satisfies the integral condition.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification:\n- Representation: Piecewise constant function over N grid points, dx=2/N\n- Variables: h \u2208 [0,1]^N\n- Objective: min max_k \u2211_{i,j} h[i] * (1-h[j+k]) * indicator(j+k within bounds) * dx\n- Constraints: \n  \u2211 h[i] * dx = 1 (integral constraint)\n  0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1\n- Projection Operator: \u03a0(h) projects h to satisfy constraints by clipping and mass preservation\n- Temperature Schedule: T(t) = initial_T * (1 - cooling_rate * t)\n- Fitness Function: based on the autocorrelation maxima scaled by dx\n\n3. Implementation Procedure:\n- Initialize:\n  - GridResolutions = [4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256, 512, 400]\n  - Start with appropriate projection of initial_h_values\n  - Define base_optimizer = 'SLSQP' and refinement_optimizer = 'simulated_annealing'\n\n- Multi-resolution Optimization Loop:\n  1. Adapt grid resolution based on current score\n  2. Coarse grid exploration: use grid size resolved_index-1\n  3. Fine grid refinement: use grid size resolved_index+1\n  4. Project solution between resolutions ensuring mass preservation\n  5. Update_best_solution if new best found\n\n- Fitness Evaluation:\n  - Compute autocorrelation for (fine grid) representation\n  - Scale by dx and select maxima\n  - Use as objective for minimization (lower is better)\n\n4. Search Choices and Variations:\n- Grid Resolution Schedule:\n  InitialGrid = 64\n  ExpansionCDF = [0.9, 0.7, 0.5, 0.3, 0.2] for grid sizes [128, 256, 512, 400]\n  Step sizes = 6 (for sampling spacewalk interval)\n\n- Optimization Parameters:\n  TemplateParams = {\n      'niter': 500000,\n      'alpha': 500000,\n      'mu': 0.92,\n      'clip_first': 0.95,\n      'learning_rate': 0.92,\n      'start_cond': 'explore'\n  }\n\n- Temperature Management:\n  BaseTemp = 0.3\n  CoolingRate = 0.001\n  Rewarm Probabilities:\n    TemperatureReset = {0.95: 0.99, 0.9: 0.95, 0.85: 0.9, 0.8: 0.99}\n\n5. Compute Budget and Robustness:\n- Total Iterations: 900000\n- Key Checkpoints:\n  - Unit testing at iterations 100k, 200k, 300k\n  - Cooldowns between resolution changes: 500 steps\n  - Warm-up phasers at 90% of grid resolution steps\n- Timeout Structure:\n  - Budget allocation: 50% for grid search, 40% for refinement\n  - Early termination if no improvement last 10 temperature resets\n  - Stall protection: restart mechanism on cumulative plateau\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract:\n- Entanglement Checks:\n  Topology_INTEGRAL = (np.isclose(sum(h)_adjusted, 1) [within 1e-7]\n  Topology_DOMAIN = (all(h[i]) between 0 and 1)\n  Topology_OBJECTIVE = (score within finite range)\n- Check Mechanisms:\n  SeedCheck = np.random.RandomState(seed) for consistent results\n  ScoreClamp = float('-inf') to 0.55  (lower is better, 0.38 is target)\n  RebuildFallback = [quadratic, tent, interpolated_parent] solutions if:\n      (1) Any constraint violated || \n      (2) C5 score exceeds threshold",
